The verse you've quoted is from the Dhammapada (Pali), the verse "Taṃ vo vadāmi bhaddaṃ vo, yāvantettha samāgatā; Taṇhāya mūlaṃ khaṇatha, usīrattho'va bīraṇaṃ" which is found in the Jātaka commentary/Sutta tradition as a verse addressed to assembled listeners. In the Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (VRI) edition, the full verse reads:

**Taṃ vo vadāmi bhaddaṃ vo, yāvantettha samāgatā;
Taṇhāya mūlaṃ khaṇatha, usīrattho'va bīraṇaṃ.
Mā vo naḷaṃva sotova, māro bhañji punappunaṃ.**

